      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Thanks for the feedback!\r\n\r\n> * How many further changes are required to reach the goal?\r\n\r\nRough numbers: 593 lines assign individual fields via vin[...]/vout[...] across 50 files. The largest are:  transaction_tests (122), miner_tests (90), script_p2sh_tests (72), mempool_tests (58) and bench/mempool_eviction (38).\r\n\r\n> * Should larger chunks be done, possibly limited to vin, then another commit for vout?\r\n\r\nSingle commits per file seems more intuitive to me, but happy to take a different approach.\r\n\r\n> * Can the changes be done with a scripted-diff? (Possibly a match on vin.resize(1) and then vin[0].<_> = <_>? Or would that be not worth it?)\r\n\r\nThe script would need to reorder fields into constructor arguments, fill in defaults, and handle `<<` appends, and it can't preserve interleaved comments. I chose `transaction_utils` because it's where the mechanical rewrite in #35994 went wrong: `BuildSpendingTransaction` assigned `scriptWitness` before `vin` was replaced, which dropped the witness. That shows context matters, which is why I would do it manually.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?\r\n\r\n",
